In Castner - Kellner cell, Reaction at anode is

\mathrm{Cl}^{-} \longrightarrow \frac{1}{2} \mathrm{Cl}_2+e^{-}

Reaction cathode is

\begin{aligned}
\mathrm{Na}^{+}+e^{-} & \longrightarrow \mathrm{Na} \\
2 \mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O}+2 e^{-} & \longrightarrow 2 \mathrm{OH}^{-}+\mathrm{H}_2 \uparrow
\end{aligned}

Hence, in Castner-Kellner cell $\mathrm{NaOH}$ is produced by $\mathrm{NaCl}$ solution.

Hence, option (a) is correct.

